From: gstreamer-custom-build local patches
Subject: [PATCH] vampeg2dec: report INTERLEAVED for consistently ordered interlaced streams

vampeg2dec derived interlace-mode from the sequence extension alone: any
stream with progressive_sequence == 0 was reported as
GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_MIXED, no matter how uniform the pictures actually
are.

"mixed" means "frames may be progressive or interlaced, and this can change
per buffer", which is a much weaker guarantee than a plain interlaced stream
and forces every downstream element onto the per-buffer-flag path (see
gst_va_buffer_get_surface_flags(), and the d3d11compositor case in
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/work_items/5088).
Ordinary broadcast MPEG-2 — frame pictures with progressive_frame == 0 and a
constant top_field_first — is a consistently ordered interlaced stream and
should be reported as GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_INTERLEAVED.

This is the MPEG-2 counterpart of
0004-vah264dec-report-interleaved-for-consistent-PAFF.patch, which made the
same distinction for H.264 PAFF streams; see
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/work_items/5011

The sequence starts out optimistically assuming INTERLEAVED, and
gst_va_mpeg2_dec_update_interlace_mode(), called for every picture from
start_picture(), falls back to MIXED (sticky for the sequence, with a
re-negotiation) as soon as the stream stops being uniform:

  * progressive_frame == 1, i.e. a progressive frame among interlaced ones,
  * a field-coded picture (picture_structure != FRAME), whose field parity is
    given by picture_structure rather than top_field_first and is therefore
    better described per buffer,
  * a change of the top_field_first ordering.

Verified on an Intel i5-7260U iGPU with a 720x480i MPEG-2 stream received
over RTP/MPEG-2 PS: the decoder now negotiates interlace-mode=interleaved and
no fallback to mixed is triggered.

Note that field-order is intentionally left out of the caps (as in the H.264
patch): gst_va_base_dec_set_output_state() builds the output state from the
interlace mode only, so GST_VIDEO_INFO_FIELD_ORDER() would not reach the
caps. The field order is carried per buffer by GST_VIDEO_BUFFER_FLAG_TFF,
which 0006-mpeg2decoder-flag-interlaced-frame-pictures.patch makes correct
for frame pictures.

--- a/_p2_/sys/va/gstvampeg2dec.c
+++ b/_p2_/sys/va/gstvampeg2dec.c
@@ -72,6 +72,18 @@
 
   gboolean progressive;
   GstMpegVideoSequenceHdr seq;
+
+  /* Local fix: track whether the pictures actually decoded so far form a
+   * consistently ordered interlaced stream (truly INTERLEAVED) instead of
+   * always reporting GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_MIXED whenever
+   * progressive_sequence == 0. See gst_va_mpeg2_dec_update_interlace_mode()
+   * and gst_va_mpeg2_dec_new_sequence().
+   * Upstream tracking: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/work_items/5011
+   */
+  gboolean have_interlacing_info;
+  gboolean field_order_known;
+  gboolean top_field_first;
+  GstVideoInterlaceMode resolved_interlace_mode;
 };
 
 static GstElementClass *parent_class = NULL;
@@ -85,6 +97,11 @@
 
 static const gchar *sink_caps_str = "video/x-mpeg2";
 
+/* Local fix: forward declaration, see definition and struct comment
+ * above for rationale. */
+static void gst_va_mpeg2_dec_update_interlace_mode (GstVaMpeg2Dec * self,
+    const GstMpegVideoPictureExt * pic_ext);
+
 static VAProfile
 _map_profile (GstMpegVideoProfile profile)
 {
@@ -222,8 +239,22 @@
   progressive = seq_ext ? seq_ext->progressive : 1;
   if (self->progressive != progressive) {
     self->progressive = progressive;
-    GST_VIDEO_INFO_INTERLACE_MODE (info) = progressive ?
-        GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_PROGRESSIVE : GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_MIXED;
+
+    /* Local fix: do not immediately assume MIXED for a non-progressive
+     * sequence. Start by optimistically assuming a consistently ordered
+     * true interlaced (INTERLEAVED) stream, and let
+     * gst_va_mpeg2_dec_update_interlace_mode() (called for every picture
+     * from start_picture()) downgrade to MIXED only when the pictures
+     * really are mixed: a progressive_frame showing up, a field-coded
+     * picture, or a change in top_field_first ordering. See the struct
+     * comment above for the rationale. */
+    self->have_interlacing_info = !progressive;
+    self->field_order_known = FALSE;
+    self->resolved_interlace_mode = progressive ?
+        GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_PROGRESSIVE :
+        GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_INTERLEAVED;
+
+    GST_VIDEO_INFO_INTERLACE_MODE (info) = self->resolved_interlace_mode;
     negotiation_needed = TRUE;
     GST_INFO_OBJECT (self, "Interlaced mode changed to %d", !progressive);
   }
@@ -360,6 +391,71 @@
       VAIQMatrixBufferType, &iq_matrix, sizeof (iq_matrix));
 }
 
+/* Local fix: for non-progressive sequences (progressive_sequence == 0) the
+ * previous code in gst_va_mpeg2_dec_new_sequence() unconditionally reported
+ * GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_MIXED. "mixed" means "each buffer may be
+ * progressive or interlaced", which is a much weaker guarantee than a plain
+ * interlaced stream, and it forces every downstream element to rely on the
+ * per-buffer GST_VIDEO_BUFFER_FLAG_INTERLACED / _TFF flags. Ordinary
+ * broadcast MPEG-2 (e.g. 720x480i or 1920x1080i, frame pictures with
+ * progressive_frame == 0 and a constant top_field_first) is a consistently
+ * ordered interlaced stream and should be reported as
+ * GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_INTERLEAVED instead.
+ *
+ * This mirrors the same distinction made for H.264 PAFF streams in
+ * 0004-vah264dec-report-interleaved-for-consistent-PAFF.patch; see
+ * https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/work_items/5011
+ *
+ * We inspect the picture coding extension of every picture and fall back to
+ * MIXED as soon as the stream stops being uniform:
+ *
+ *   * progressive_frame == 1, i.e. a progressive frame among interlaced ones,
+ *   * a field-coded picture (picture_structure != FRAME), whose field parity
+ *     comes from picture_structure rather than top_field_first, so it is
+ *     described per buffer instead,
+ *   * a change of the top_field_first ordering.
+ *
+ * The decision is sticky: once MIXED, it stays MIXED for the sequence. */
+static void
+gst_va_mpeg2_dec_update_interlace_mode (GstVaMpeg2Dec * self,
+    const GstMpegVideoPictureExt * pic_ext)
+{
+  gboolean top_field_first;
+
+  if (!self->have_interlacing_info
+      || self->resolved_interlace_mode == GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_MIXED)
+    return;
+
+  if (pic_ext->progressive_frame) {
+    GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (self, "Progressive frame found in an interlaced "
+        "sequence, falling back to interlace-mode=mixed");
+    self->resolved_interlace_mode = GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_MIXED;
+    return;
+  }
+
+  if (pic_ext->picture_structure != GST_MPEG_VIDEO_PICTURE_STRUCTURE_FRAME) {
+    GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (self, "Field-coded picture (picture_structure %d), "
+        "falling back to interlace-mode=mixed", pic_ext->picture_structure);
+    self->resolved_interlace_mode = GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_MIXED;
+    return;
+  }
+
+  top_field_first = (pic_ext->top_field_first != 0);
+
+  if (!self->field_order_known) {
+    self->field_order_known = TRUE;
+    self->top_field_first = top_field_first;
+    return;
+  }
+
+  if (self->top_field_first != top_field_first) {
+    GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (self, "Field order changed (top-field-first %d -> %d), "
+        "falling back to interlace-mode=mixed", self->top_field_first,
+        top_field_first);
+    self->resolved_interlace_mode = GST_VIDEO_INTERLACE_MODE_MIXED;
+  }
+}
+
 static inline uint32_t
 _is_frame_start (GstMpeg2Picture * picture)
 {
@@ -392,6 +488,24 @@
   GstVaDecodePicture *va_pic;
   VAPictureParameterBufferMPEG2 pic_param;
 
+  /* Local fix: refine interlace-mode using the picture coding extensions
+   * seen so far (see gst_va_mpeg2_dec_update_interlace_mode() and the
+   * struct comment above). Re-negotiate if the resolved mode differs from
+   * what was last reported on the output caps. */
+  if (self->have_interlacing_info) {
+    gst_va_mpeg2_dec_update_interlace_mode (self, slice->pic_ext);
+
+    if (GST_VIDEO_INFO_INTERLACE_MODE (&base->output_info) !=
+        self->resolved_interlace_mode) {
+      GST_INFO_OBJECT (self,
+          "Refining interlace-mode to %d based on the observed pictures",
+          self->resolved_interlace_mode);
+      GST_VIDEO_INFO_INTERLACE_MODE (&base->output_info) =
+          self->resolved_interlace_mode;
+      base->need_negotiation = TRUE;
+    }
+  }
+
   va_pic = gst_mpeg2_picture_get_user_data (picture);
 
   /* *INDENT-OFF* */
